[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z ## 15. Glossary
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Term | Definition |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z |------|------------|
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Case | One exam or course board, containing cards and connections. Cards belong to exactly one case. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Card | A Study Note, Source, or Topic hub pinned to a case board. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Study Note | A photo card representing notes the student wrote, with a short title. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Source / Evidence | A photo card representing the original material a note came from. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Topic hub | A text-only card representing a theme or exam topic. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Association string | A red, undirected connection between two cards, usually a note and a topic. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Provenance string | A thin dashed amber connection between a Study Note and a Source. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Loose thread | A Study Note missing a provenance link or a topic association, or a Topic with no connections. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Ready | A case with zero loose threads; the only state in which it can be closed. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Closed | A case the student marked complete. It stays editable and can be reopened. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Recall mode | A non-persistent review mode that hides strings and checks connections the student redraws from memory. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Case shelf | The home screen listing all cases. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | `.ndcase` | The single-case ZIP backup format. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | Demo case | A locally generated, clearly labeled sample case that can be removed and is never reseeded automatically. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z ---
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z ## 16. Open Questions
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | # | Question | Default Assumption |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z |---|----------|--------------------|
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 1 | Which early graphical detective games are the aesthetic reference? | The visual-direction spike presents three options; the human review records the choice. The fallback is cork, sepia, oxblood, and period headings only. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 2 | What should pins, string sag, and lift feel like? | Brass pins, 3px red string with 12px sag, dashed amber provenance. The board-feel human review can revise it before closure work. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 3 | Is handwriting OCR accurate enough to be useful? | Ship it off by default, user-triggered, title prefill only, never overwrite edits, never auto-tag. Reassess after real use. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 4 | Should case archives be encrypted? | V1 archives are unencrypted ZIPs with a warning; encryption is future work. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 5 | Should whole-library export exist? | Deferred; v1 exports exactly one case at a time. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 6 | What happens when a closed case is edited into loose threads? | Keep `closedAt`, show `Closed · loose threads`, and require a fresh close after repair; never auto-reopen. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 7 | Can a removed demo case be restored? | No automatic reseed; the student can create a new case. A manual restore action can be added later. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:18:32.637Z | 8 | Are reminders or exam-date notifications in scope? | No notifications in v1; the exam date is display and sort metadata only. |
