[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 93-## 4. UI / Interaction Design
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 94-
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 95-- The shelf is the home route. It shows a responsive grid of case cards, an empty state with a single primary action, and a compact storage status strip.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 96-- A case card shows title, subject, exam date, card count, connection count, readiness/closure badge, and last modified. The whole card is a link; edit and delete are separate buttons with 44px targets that do not nest inside the link.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 97-- Create and edit use a dialog with title, subject, and optional exam date. Title validation is inline and announced. Escape cancels; focus returns to the trigger.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 98-- Delete uses a destructive confirmation dialog that states exactly how many cards, strings, and images will be removed. There is no undo for case deletion; the dialog says so.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 99-- Storage status shows `Persistent` or `Best effort`, a usage bar, and a warning above 80 percent. When persistence is denied, the backup prompt is more prominent on the shelf and case screen.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DATA-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T20:28:08.027Z 100-- Multi-tab refresh is silent: another tab's mutation invalidates the shelf and current case summary. A form being edited is never overwritten by a background refresh.
