[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.407Z | [VIS-CON-02](#VIS-CON-02) | No accounts or telemetry | Must |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.407Z | [VIS-CON-11](#VIS-CON-11) | Validate imports and prevent archive path traversal | Must |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.407Z | [VIS-CON-12](#VIS-CON-12) | Avoid injection from titles, tags, OCR text, and archive metadata | Must |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.407Z | [VIS-CON-13](#VIS-CON-13) | Release user content only by explicit user action | Must |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.407Z ```forge-requirement
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z {"id":"VIS-CON-11","kind":"constraint","text":"Validate every imported archive entry, manifest field, checksum, and path before writing; reject absolute paths, traversal, duplicate entries, oversized entries, and unsupported versions."}
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```forge-requirement
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z {"id":"VIS-CON-12","kind":"constraint","text":"Render all user-supplied and imported text as text, never as HTML; do not use dangerouslySetInnerHTML for titles, tags, OCR, or manifest content."}
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```forge-requirement
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z {"id":"VIS-CON-13","kind":"constraint","text":"Write a backup or download a file only after an explicit user action; never auto-export or auto-share."}
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z Supporting decisions:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - No authentication is required because there is no server and no multi-user boundary. Device access is the security boundary.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - The case archive is an unencrypted ZIP. The app warns that it contains private notes and asks the student to store it somewhere they trust. Encryption is a future consideration.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - The app does not log image contents, OCR text, or titles to the console in production.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - Object URLs for images are revoked when a view unmounts or a replacement succeeds.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - GitHub Pages cannot set custom response headers, so the plan does not claim a strict CSP. It does ensure no inline event handlers, no third-party scripts, and same-origin assets only.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ## 10. System States / Lifecycle
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ### 10.1 Case Lifecycle
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z (no cases) -> demo seeded once -> open case -> [readiness: ready | loose threads]
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z                                       |                         |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z                                       +---- close (only ready) -+
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z                                                                  |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z                                       closed case <---- reopen ---+
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z                                       (still editable; readiness recomputed)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - A case is `open` or `closed`; `closedAt` is metadata, never a lock.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - Readiness is derived on every read: `ready` when there are zero loose threads, otherwise `loose`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - A closed case whose edits create loose threads displays `Closed · loose threads` and offers close again after repair; it does not silently reopen.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - Manual reopen clears `closedAt` after confirmation. There is no automatic reopen or archiving.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ### 10.2 Board and Recall States
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z shelf -> board (pan/zoom/edit) -> capture -> board
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z board -> recall -> draw scratch -> check -> results -> exit (scratch discarded)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z board -> export -> file; shelf -> import -> copy (default) | replace (explicit)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - Recall state is in memory only. A reload, exit, or route change discards the scratch layer.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - A case's last viewport is restored on return. Recall entry fits the case to view without mutating the stored viewport.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ### 10.3 Storage States
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - `persistent`: the browser granted persistent storage.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - `best-effort`: the request was denied or unsupported; the UI shows the backup reminder prominently.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - `warning`: usage exceeds 80% of the reported quota.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z - `error`: IndexedDB cannot open or a read fails; the shelf shows a recoverable error with Retry and import guidance instead of a silently empty shelf.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-25T21:35:59.408Z ---
