[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z ## 4. UI / Interaction Design
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z - Export is available from a case and from the shelf row menu. It opens a save dialog or triggers a download named `<case-slug>-<yyyy-mm-dd>.ndcase`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z - Import is available from the shelf. The file picker accepts `.ndcase`. After validation, a summary shows case title, card count, connection count, image count, and exported date.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z - Default action is `Restore as a copy`. If an archived case ID already exists, a secondary `Replace existing case` option appears with the existing title and requires a typed confirmation.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z - Progress is stage-based: Reading archive, Checking integrity, Restoring images, Restoring cards, Done. Errors name the failed stage and keep the existing data untouched.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z - Success shows `Open case` and `Back to shelf`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z - The backup reminder appears as a non-blocking banner on the case screen when the case first reaches 5 cards and 1 connection. `Back up now` opens export; `Not now` dismisses for that case permanently. It never blocks editing.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z - The archive contains private notes. The UI states that the file is not encrypted and should be stored somewhere trusted.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=BACKUP-4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T04:40:16.359Z ---
