[engine] harness activity stdout task=LINK-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:25:28.492Z - `ThreadAnchor` is a Pixi interaction target mounted through `CardSprite` at the card’s right edge, shown for the selected/hovered card. The DOM hit test uses a constant 22 px screen radius (44 px target), including when zoomed out.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=LINK-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:25:28.492Z - Hover or touch selection reveals the anchor. Dragging from it draws the screen-space red draft thread (12 px sag scaled by zoom at 100%, capped at 25% of pull distance), highlights a distinct target card with a red outline, and emits a drop intent.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=LINK-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:25:28.492Z - Dropping on a card creates exactly one association (repository default), selects it, and opens the type menu. Provenance is disabled for ineligible pairs and the reason is visible plus `role="status"`/`aria-describedby` announced. Provenance retype updates the same row; dismissal keeps association.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=LINK-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:25:28.492Z - Self, empty-cork, and duplicate drops create nothing. Duplicates select the existing connection and show the duplicate toast. A repository-race duplicate also teaches the page the existing row and selects it.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=LINK-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:25:28.492Z - The menu is clamped to the viewport and scrolls within `100dvh`.
