[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z ## 4. UI / Interaction Design
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - Each card shows a small thread anchor at its right edge when selected or hovered; on touch it appears after a tap selects the card. Dragging from the anchor draws a temporary red thread that follows the pointer and highlights a valid target.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - Dropping on a valid card creates an association by default and opens a small type menu with Association and Provenance. Provenance is disabled with an explanation unless the pair is a Study Note and a Source. Dismissing the menu keeps the association.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - Dropping on the same card, empty cork, or an existing pair cancels or selects the existing string. A short toast explains a duplicate.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - Strings sag 12px at 100 percent zoom, scale with the board, and anchor at card edges. Association is 3px red; provenance is 2px dashed amber. Reduced motion removes the draw-in animation.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - Tapping a string opens a small connection detail with the two card titles, type toggle, and Delete. Delete confirmation names both cards and the type.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - The legend is a collapsible key on the board: red line = association, dashed amber = provenance. It is not a label on individual strings.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - Keyboard: from card detail or the card list, `Connect to…` opens a dialog with a searchable target list and a type radio group. Provenance filters to Sources when the current card is a Note and to Notes when it is a Source. The same dialog can change type or delete an existing connection.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z - Deleting a card already cascades its strings through BOARD-5; this feature's repository guarantees no dangling rows.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=LINK-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T06:34:42.861Z ---
