[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z ## 10. System States / Lifecycle
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z ### 10.1 Case Lifecycle
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z (no cases) -> demo seeded once -> open case -> [readiness: ready | loose threads]
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z                                       |                         |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z                                       +---- close (only ready) -+
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z                                                                  |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z                                       closed case <---- reopen ---+
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z                                       (still editable; readiness recomputed)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z - A case is `open` or `closed`; `closedAt` is metadata, never a lock.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z - Readiness is derived on every read: `ready` when there are zero loose threads, otherwise `loose`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z - A closed case whose edits create loose threads displays `Closed · loose threads` and offers close again after repair; it does not silently reopen.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z - Manual reopen clears `closedAt` after confirmation. There is no automatic reopen or archiving.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z ### 10.2 Board and Recall States
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z shelf -> board (pan/zoom/edit) -> capture -> board
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z board -> recall -> draw scratch -> check -> results -> exit (scratch discarded)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z board -> export -> file; shelf -> import -> copy (default) | replace (explicit)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T07:12:00.961Z - Recall state is in memory only. A reload, exit, or route change discards the scratch layer.
