[engine] harness activity stderr task=OCR-3 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T07:45:17.743Z     "stdout": "I'll start by reading the execution file and relevant documentation.\nNow I understand the current state. Let me make the OCR search matching bounded and whitespace-robust, and add explicit OCR preservation guards to the archive path.\nImplemented OCR-3: OCR text is now a first-class, bounded search target and OCR metadata is guarded through both archive directions.\n\n## Task IDs\n\n- **OCR-3** — Include OCR text in search and case archives (OCR-FR-05, OCR-FR-04, OCR-CON-02, SEARCH-CON-03).\n- No domain schema, Dexie migration, or archive format-version change was required. OCR fields were already optional members of `cardRecordSchema`; this task made their search and archive behavior explicit and test-enforced.\n\n## Files created or changed\n\n**Changed**\n- `src/features/search/searchCards.ts`\n- `src/features/backup/archiveFormat.ts`\n- `src/features/backup/exportCase.ts`\n- `src/features/backup/importCase.ts`\n\n**Created**\n- `tests/search/ocrSearch.test.ts`\n- `tests/backup/ocrRoundTrip.test.ts`\n\n## Invariants and failure modes covered\n\n**Search**\n- OCR phrases match case-insensitively and return a snippet containing the phrase.\n- Snippet body is hard-capped at `OCR_SNIPPET_MAX_LENGTH = 160` characters, plus at most two ellipses; a 300-character query still produces a bounded result.\n- OCR whitespace is collapsed before matching, so text split by newlines, tabs, or repeated spaces is findable with a normal single-space query.\n- Cards with no OCR fields do not throw, are not matched by OCR, and still match by title/tag.\n- Confidence, engine version, OCR timestamp, card ID, position, and type are not searchable.\n- Search leaves card arrays, tags, types, and serialized card data unchanged; it creates no tags, connections, or card types.\n\n**Archive**\n- Export writes `ocrText`, `ocrConfidence`, `ocrEngineVersion`, and `ocrUpdatedAt` into the manifest card