[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ## 10. System States / Lifecycle
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ### 10.1 Case Lifecycle
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z (no cases) -> demo seeded once -> open case -> [readiness: ready | loose threads]
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z                                       |                         |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z                                       +---- close (only ready) -+
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z                                                                  |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z                                       closed case <---- reopen ---+
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z                                       (still editable; readiness recomputed)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - A case is `open` or `closed`; `closedAt` is metadata, never a lock.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - Readiness is derived on every read: `ready` when there are zero loose threads, otherwise `loose`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - A closed case whose edits create loose threads displays `Closed · loose threads` and offers close again after repair; it does not silently reopen.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - Manual reopen clears `closedAt` after confirmation. There is no automatic reopen or archiving.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ### 10.2 Board and Recall States
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z shelf -> board (pan/zoom/edit) -> capture -> board
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z board -> recall -> draw scratch -> check -> results -> exit (scratch discarded)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z board -> export -> file; shelf -> import -> copy (default) | replace (explicit)
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - Recall state is in memory only. A reload, exit, or route change discards the scratch layer.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - A case's last viewport is restored on return. Recall entry fits the case to view without mutating the stored viewport.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z ### 10.3 Storage States
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - `persistent`: the browser granted persistent storage.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - `best-effort`: the request was denied or unsupported; the UI shows the backup reminder prominently.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - `warning`: usage exceeds 80% of the reported quota.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=CLOSE-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:33:31.511Z - `error`: IndexedDB cannot open or a read fails; the shelf shows a recoverable error with Retry and import guidance instead of a silently empty shelf.
