[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z ### What was implemented
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - **`recallStore.ts`**
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Vanilla Zustand in-memory store (`createStore` from `zustand/vanilla`) with singleton `recallStore` and isolated `createRecallStore()`.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - `addScratchConnection`, `removeScratchConnection`, `removeScratchConnectionForPair`, `clearScratch`, and `resetOnExit`.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Scratch pairs are canonicalized with the domain `buildPairKey`; the pair key is the scratch string ID. A duplicate draw in either orientation returns the existing row.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Rejects self-links, empty endpoints, and unknown relationship types without changing state.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Selectors for scratch connections, count, presence, and lookup.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - No Dexie, repository, IndexedDB, localStorage, persist middleware, React, or PixiJS imports.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - **`compareConnections.ts`**
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - `compareConnections(truth, scratch)` returns exactly `remembered`, `missed`, `extra`, and `typeMismatch`.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Matching is undirected; a reversed scratch pair counts as remembered.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - A wrong-type pair is remembered and listed in `typeMismatch`, never in `missed`; explicit `expectedType` and `actualType` are returned.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Duplicate input rows collapse to one output entry per pair. Every group is sorted by canonical pair key; no score, percentage, grade, streak, or ranking exists in the result.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Invalid rows are ignored rather than crashing a recall check.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z   - Exports `canonicalizeConnection` and `canonicalizeConnections` for result rendering and future tasks.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z ### Verification exercised
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - Empty truth/scratch → four empty groups.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - Exact, reversed, duplicate, extra, and missed pairs.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - Type mismatch in both orientations and suppression when an exact-type scratch row also exists.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - Stable canonical ordering and disjoint missed/extra/type-mismatch outputs.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - Duplicate representative-type selection independent of input order.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - Store add/duplicate/remove/clear/reset behavior and isolation between store instances.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=RECALL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T16:43:15.001Z - Write-spy test asserting zero calls to `IDBFactory.open`, `IDBDatabase.transaction`, IDB object-store read/write methods, `Storage` mutations, and every `ConnectionRepository` / `InMemoryConnectionRepository` method during enter, draw, check, remove, reset, and exit.
