[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-1 attempt=2 at=2026-10-26T16:44:06.093Z     "stdout": "## Result Report\n\n**Task:** RECALL-1 — Implement scratch connections and recall comparison  \n**Owner:** board-engineer\n\n### Files created\n\n- `src/features/recall/recallStore.ts`\n- `src/features/recall/compareConnections.ts`\n- `tests/recall/compareConnections.test.ts`\n- `tests/recall/recallStore.test.ts`\n\nNo existing shared files were modified. `CaseBoardPage.tsx`, `routes.tsx`, and all storage/bundle-boundary files are untouched.\n\n### What was implemented\n\n- **`recallStore.ts`**\n  - Vanilla Zustand in-memory store (`createStore` from `zustand/vanilla`) with singleton `recallStore` and isolated `createRecallStore()`.\n  - `addScratchConnection`, `removeScratchConnection`, `removeScratchConnectionForPair`, `clearScratch`, and `resetOnExit`.\n  - Scratch pairs are canonicalized with the domain `buildPairKey`; the pair key is the scratch string ID. A duplicate draw in either orientation returns the existing row.\n  - Rejects self-links, empty endpoints, and unknown relationship types without changing state.\n  - Selectors for scratch connections, count, presence, and lookup.\n  - No Dexie, repository, IndexedDB, localStorage, persist middleware, React, or PixiJS imports.\n\n- **`compareConnections.ts`**\n  - `compareConnections(truth, scratch)` returns exactly `remembered`, `missed`, `extra`, and `typeMismatch`.\n  - Matching is undirected; a reversed scratch pair counts as remembered.\n  - A wrong-type pair is remembered and listed in `typeMismatch`, never in `missed`; explicit `expectedType` and `actualType` are returned.\n  - Duplicate input rows collapse to one output entry per pair. Every group is sorted by canonical pair key; no score, percentage, grade, streak, or ranking exists in the result.\n  - Invalid rows are ignored rather than crashing a recall check.\n  - Exports `canonicalizeConnection` and `canonicalizeConnections` for result rendering and future tasks.\n\n### Verification exercised\n\n- Empty truth/scratch → four empty groups.\n- Exact, reversed, duplicate, extra, and missed pairs.\n- Type mismatch in both orientations and suppression when an exact-type scratch row also exists.\n- Stable canonical ordering and disjoint missed/extra/type-mismatch outputs.\n- Duplicate representative-type selection independent of input order.\n- Store add/duplicate/remove/clear/reset behavior and isolation between store instances.\n- Write-spy test asserting zero calls to `IDBFactory.open`, `IDBDatabase.transaction`, IDB object-store read/write methods, `Storage` mutations, and every `ConnectionRepository` / `InMemoryConnectionRepository` method during enter, draw, check, remove, reset, and exit.\n- Module-boundary source checks for forbidden storage, repository, React, PixiJS, and persist imports.\n- A guard sanity test confirms the localStorage spy observes a real write.\n\n### Validation results\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm test -- tests/recall/compareConnections.test.ts tests/recall/recallStore.test.ts` | **33 tests passed** |\n| `npm run typecheck` | **Passed, zero errors** |\n| `npm test` (full suite) | **66 files / 871 tests passed** |\n| Targeted ESLint + Prettier check | **Passed** |\n\n### Contract for downstream tasks\n\n- **Consumed snapshot:** none. These modules consume only plain connection-like objects; they never receive or call a repository.\n- **Board/UI integration contract:** RECALL-2 must call `recallStore.getState().resetOnExit()` on recall unmount/route change, and `useScratchConnections` can bind `selectScratchConnections`, `addScratchConnection`, and the removal actions.\n- **Results contract:** RECALL-3 can pass truth `ConnectionRecord[]` and scratch `ScratchConnection[]` directly to `compareConnections`, then map IDs to titles.\n\n### Limitations\n\n- RECALL-1 is unit-only by design; no browser gesture or visual evidence applies to this task.\n- The recall page, toolbar, scratch string rendering, and results panel remain RECALL-2/RECALL-3 scope.\n\n```forge-…[truncated 1708 chars]
