[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z /**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * Pure comparison for recall mode.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * Recall practice is undirected: a scratch string drawn B-to-A is the same
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * relationship as a truth string stored A-to-B. This module canonicalizes both
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * sides by sorted card IDs, matches each truth pair against the scratch layer,
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * and returns four separate lists:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * - `remembered`: truth pairs the student reproduced.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * - `missed`: truth pairs with no scratch string.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * - `extra`: scratch strings that do not correspond to any truth pair.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * - `typeMismatch`: remembered pairs whose relationship type differs.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * There is deliberately no score, percentage, grade, streak, or rank in the
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * result. Counts are the lengths of the lists. Ordering is stable: every list
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * is sorted by canonical pair key, and a pair appears at most once in a list.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * Boundary rules:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * - No Dexie, IndexedDB, localStorage, repository, React, or PixiJS import.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * - No mutation of the supplied arrays or records.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.449Z  * - Invalid rows (empty IDs, self-links, unknown types) are ignored rather
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z  *   than crashing a recall check on a hand-edited snapshot.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z  */
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z import { CONNECTION_TYPES, buildPairKey } from '../../domain/model';
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z import type { ConnectionType } from '../../domain/model';
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z /** The minimum truth or scratch shape needed to compare two endpoints. */
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z export interface ComparableConnection {
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z   readonly fromCardId: string;
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z   readonly toCardId: string;
[engine] harness activity stderr task=RECALL-3 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T17:38:46.450Z   readonly type: ConnectionType;
