[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 107-- Breakpoints: phone below 600px, tablet 600–1199px, desktop 1200px and up. The primary design target is 1280x800 landscape. Phone keeps every capability but turns side panels into bottom sheets and collapses the board toolbar to one trigger.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 108-- Safe-area insets are applied to the top bar, bottom toolbar, and sheets so notched phones do not hide controls. No screen uses a fixed width that causes page-level horizontal scrolling; the board itself pans inside its own viewport.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 109-- The keyboard path is a first-class route set, not a hidden accessibility mode: Case list, Card detail, Connection picker, Search, Recall. Shortcuts include `?` for help, `/` for search, `[`/`]` for previous/next card, `c` to connect, and `Escape` to close.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 110-- A `Keyboard shortcuts` panel in Settings lists every shortcut and a short description. A `Skip to case content` link is present on every case screen.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 111-- The canvas has `role="img"` or an equivalent labeled region with a description such as `Case board with 24 cards arranged spatially. Use the card list for a keyboard-operable view.` A visible `Open card list` action sits next to the board controls.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 112-- The motion toggle is in Settings under Appearance. It defaults to the system preference and persists an explicit override. Changing it applies immediately without reload.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 113-- Browser notice: if IndexedDB, Web Workers, WebAssembly, or service workers are missing, a non-blocking top banner explains which feature is reduced and links to the support matrix. The app still renders the shelf and any available data.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=A11Y-4 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T19:34:22.935Z 114-- Performance: the board culls, uses thumbnails first, caps resident textures, and reports a development-only frame summary. The automated harness seeds 150 cards, pans for five seconds, and records p95 frame time and average FPS.
