[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z ### Defects and residual risk
[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z **No blocking defect found for the A11Y-5 acceptance criteria.**
[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z Residual risks, all explicitly documented in `docs/quality/performance-budget.md`:
[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z - The automated CI floor runs at a **75% detail camera** (8 visible cards on tablet/desktop). The 150-card graph, all card sprites, culling, camera transforms, and Pixi render path are real, but a dense zoomed-out overview with 20+ visible cards is **not** gated by the 30 FPS floor. The 45 FPS target must be measured by a human on the target tablet, including a zoomed-out view.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z - The fixture has no images, OCR text, or strings; texture residency and string-layer volume remain human-review risks.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z - Headless software WebGL is host-load sensitive. The suite now uses one worker so parallel WebGL contexts do not corrupt the measurement.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z - The **45 FPS tablet target is explicitly deferred** to the final human tablet review. The automated spec records this deferral in every evidence attachment and never claims the 45 FPS result.
[engine] harness activity stdout task=A11Y-5 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:22:07.270Z - The **3-second cold load on a 20 Mbps tablet profile** is documented with its measurement method but is also deferred to field/human review; it is not represented by the local preview server.
