tor.tsx` — editor**\n- `react-easy-crop` stage with a dark mat and visible corner frame marks.\n- Touch pan and pinch/scroll zoom.\n- Rotate left/right in exact 90° steps.\n- Rotation-aware crop-frame aspect, with an optional pinned `aspect` (for example square).\n- Keyboard nudge pad and native arrow-key panning on the focusable crop area.\n- Reset, Cancel, and Save; no storage, repository, network, object-URL, or pipeline calls.\n- Polite, atomic live summary of crop percentages and rotation.\n- 44px controls, visible focus rings, semantic fieldset/legend, and reduced-motion handling.\n\n### UI handoff contract\n```ts\n<CropRotateEditor\n  imageSrc={previewUrl}\n  sourceWidth={orientedWidth}\n  sourceHeight={orientedHeight}\n  initialCrop={card?.crop}              // source-frame, normalized 0-1\n  initialRotation={card?.rotation}      // 0 | 90 | 180 | 270\n  aspect={undefined}                    // omit for free rotation-aware frame, or 1 for square\n  nudgeStep={0.02}\n  title=\"Crop and rotate\"\n  imageAlt=\"Photo to crop and rotate\"\n  saveLabel=\"Save crop\"\n  onSave={(result) => { /* result.crop, result.rotation */ }}\n  onCancel={() => { /* return to capture or card detail */ }}\n/>\n```\n\n`onSave` receives exactly:\n```ts\n{\n  crop: { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number }; // source-frame, 0-1\n  rotation: 0 | 90 | 180 | 270;\n}\n```\n\nThe editor is synchronous and has no abort state. The parent owns the preview object URL, the retained original, source dimensions, pipeline execution, and persistence. Invalid crop/rotation props fall back safely rather than throwing; pure-helper callers receive `RangeError` for invalid values. Reset restores the selection the editor opened with: full/upright at import, stored crop on card detail.\n\n### Validation evidence\nCommands run from the project root:\n\n- `npm test -- tests/capture/cropMath.test.ts tests/capture/CropRotateEditor.test.tsx` → **49 tests passed, exit 0**\n- `npm run typecheck` → **exit 0**\n- `npm test` (full suite) → **379 tests passed, 26 files, exit 0**\n-…[truncated 4398 chars]
