[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z ## 4. UI / Interaction Design
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z - There is no release UI beyond the app itself. The release artifacts are the GitHub Pages URL, the local preview command, the PWA install prompt, and the documentation.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z - The PWA install path is browser-native. On iOS Safari, the README explains Add to Home Screen; on Android and desktop, the install prompt or browser menu is documented.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z - Offline behavior is explicit: after the first successful load, the shelf, demo, board, recall, search, and OCR assets work without a network. A blocking first load without network is not possible and is documented.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z - The update prompt is the existing `UpdatePrompt`; release verification confirms it appears for a waiting worker and does not activate during an open form.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z - Release docs include a short `Known limitations` section: spatial editing is pointer-only; OCR is English and handwriting-dependent; archives are unencrypted; GitHub Pages cannot set custom security headers; browser storage may still be evicted.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z - The final review is a checklist, not a demo. It records device, browser, URL, what was exercised, pass/fail per step, and the honest would-you-use-it answer.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-1 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T20:48:44.140Z ---
