[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z The composition root is `src/main.tsx` → `src/App.tsx`, which mounts `AppBootstrap`, `AppShell`, and `src/app/routes.tsx`. Every feature screen is reachable through that router; the PixiJS board is a lazy route-level chunk.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z ### 6.3 Key APIs / Interfaces
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z - `CaseRepository` is the only write boundary for cases, cards, connections, and attachments. React code never opens Dexie directly.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z - `AttachmentStore` reads and writes original, display, and thumbnail Blobs by attachment ID and enforces replace/delete cleanup after a successful transaction.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z - `BoardScene` owns Pixi objects and reads a plain board snapshot; it never writes storage. Gesture handlers emit intents to the board store.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z - `compareConnections(truth, scratch)` is a pure function used by recall results.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z - `computeReadiness(cards, connections)` is a pure function used by closure and badges.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z - `exportCase(caseId)` and `importCase(blob, mode)` are the backup boundary; neither touches the network.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z - `useOcr` wraps a tesseract.js worker with explicit start, cancel, timeout, and cleanup.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=REL-2 attempt=1 at=2026-10-26T21:06:33.092Z ---
